{"id": "sevt_01QfLvb6CxGiYS7CdRrJ5wyt", "content": [{"text": "**Checkout 500s: root cause is an N+1 query introduced by the checkout deploy `a3f9c21`**\n\n**Evidence**\n- **Deploy timing:** checkout deploy `a3f9c21` went out at 14:31:18. `p99_latency_ms` went from about 75 ms to about 3,850 ms at 14:31, the same minute. Error rate started at 14:40 and has stayed around 0.2\u20130.6. No other deploy lines up with this: cart, auth and inventory deployed at 09:14, 11:02 and 14:55, none near 14:31.\n- **Diff:** the commit is titled \"refactor for readability\". It replaced one batched query (`order_id IN (...)`, grouped in memory) with a loop that runs `SELECT * FROM order_items WHERE order_id = ?` once per open order.\n- **Log:**\n  - Before 14:31, checkout logs only the batched `IN (?)` query.\n  - The first per-row `order_id = ?` query is logged at 14:31:18.496, right after the deploy. There are 3,320 of these lines in the log.\n  - The 500s are `PoolTimeout` errors on `/api/checkout/validate` (26), `/summary` (25) and `/submit` (19).\n  - The log also has 70 \"DB connection pool exhausted (active=50/50, waiters=12)\" errors.\n- **Mechanism:** each summary request now makes N queries instead of 1. That holds connections longer and exhausts the 50-connection pool. Requests then time out waiting for a connection and return 500.\n\n**Ruled out:** the 6 auth `identity-provider timeout` errors start at 14:15, before the deploy. They are on auth, not checkout, and are too few to explain this.\n\n**Fix:** revert `a3f9c21`, or restore the batched `order_id__in` query with in-memory grouping.\n\n> **Root cause:** `a3f9c21` \u2014 the checkout summary refactor replaced one batched `order_items` query with a per-order query in a loop (N+1), which exhausted the DB connection pool and caused `PoolTimeout` 500s.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:50:49.156524Z", "type": "agent.message"}
